小标题和表 2 你 tex 里已经有了，所以只给正文段落：

```latex
Table~\ref{tab:e2e} reports end-to-end execution time for all five
workloads. MHOT is faster than revm on every workload, ranging from
$2.22\times$ on nft-mint to $3.84\times$ on erc20-heavy, with a geometric
mean speedup of $2.82\times$. We report the geometric mean of per-workload
speedups rather than a mean of absolute times, so that long-running
workloads do not dominate the summary statistic. The gain is not
concentrated in a single favorable case: three of the five workloads
exceed $2.9\times$, and the least favorable workload still cuts execution
time by more than half.

The spread across workloads follows how much of each workload's baseline
time MHOT is able to affect. erc20-heavy benefits most, falling from
$287.3$\,ms to $74.9$\,ms, because its execution concentrates in a small
body of transfer and approval logic that is entered repeatedly, so the
same optimized code is reused across nearly every call. uniswap-v3 and
defi-mixed have longer swap and routing paths but remain dominated by
in-contract computation, and land near the geometric mean at $2.97\times$
and $3.06\times$.
% nft-mint: 2026-09-16 新机器重跑后回来改这一句
nft-mint ($2.22\times$) and proxy-chain ($2.30\times$) gain the least:
minting is dominated by cold storage writes and proxy-chain by repeated
cross-contract dispatch, so in both a larger share of execution time falls
outside the paths MHOT optimizes. Even in these two cases MHOT more than
halves end-to-end execution time.
```

